# Build context for ops/Dockerfile.web, which is the repository root.
#
# Two reasons this matters. The obvious one is speed — without it every build ships .git,
# node_modules and the backups directory to the daemon. The one that actually matters is
# that .env sits at this root: nothing copies it into an image today, but leaving secrets
# in the build context means a future `COPY . .` bakes them into a layer of a public image.
# Excluded here so that mistake cannot be made silently.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Working artifacts and local state
backups/
.claude/
_bmad/
_bmad-output/
CLAUDE.md
LOG.md
STATE.md
invite-code.txt

# Python
backend/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Node — the image runs its own `npm ci`, so a host install would only conflict
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Nothing in the image needs these
docs/
ops/compose.verify.yml
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.prod.yml
